<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n82902" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πήδ-ημα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>, τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>leap, bound</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				95
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				305
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				833
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Andr.</u>
				1139
			</span></i>, etc., cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πηδάω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1
				</span></i>
			; <i>leaping up</i> in admiration, of an audience, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.41c
			</span></i>(pl.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>beating</i> or <i>throbbing</i> of the heart, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ μέλλον καρδία πήδημ᾽ ἔχει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ba.</u>
					1288
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐσχεσθαι καρδίαν πηδήματος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.83b
				</span></i>
			.</div>
